,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:cfad1b2cdf8e674159069fb20b211cd66f437eba4d7c49a21eb9e8aa126e196e","file":"preprints/Contact-Fano-manifolds-and-the-LeBrun-Salamon-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":75,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5c2fdddb68e77b83715698c58c884f8e654c0434e6751edc08b41d84d52d6ce0","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Contact-Fano-manifolds-and-the-LeBrun-Salamon-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:cfad1b2cdf8e674159069fb20b211cd66f437eba4d7c49a21eb9e8aa126e196e","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Contact-Fano-manifolds-and-the-LeBrun-Salamon-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L75"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{thm:projective-contact}\nLet $(X,F)$ be a smooth connected complex projective contact manifold\nof dimension $2n+1$, where $n\\geq1$. Its second Betti number determines\nthe following alternatives.\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item If $b_2(X)=1$, then $(X,F)$ is contact-isomorphic to the adjoint\nvariety $Y_{\\mathfrak g}$, with its canonical contact distribution, for\na simple complex Lie algebra $\\mathfrak g$.\n\\item If $b_2(X)\\geq2$, then there is a smooth connected complex\nprojective manifold $Z$ of dimension $n+1$ and a biholomorphism\n\\[\n X\\simeq\\PP(T^*Z).\n\\]\nHere $\\PP(T^*Z)$ parametrizes lines in cotangent spaces, equivalently\nhyperplanes in tangent spaces. This assertion identifies the underlying\nmanifolds, without imposing compatibility with the given distribution $F$.\n\\end{enumerate}\nConversely, every adjoint variety of complex dimension $2n+1$ and every\nprojectivized cotangent bundle in the second alternative admits a contact\nstructure. Thus these are precisely the underlying manifolds of smooth\nconnected complex projective contact manifolds in these dimensions."}
